WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.960
What happens to the health of
our colon within just two weeks

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:09.440
after switching from a standard American
diet to one centered around plants?

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:11.934
Watch the video to find out.

00:00:12.038 --> 00:00:18.668
"The Best Dietary Changes
for Colon Cancer Prevention"

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:23.480
We have 100 trillion micro-organisms
residing in our gut,

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:27.440
give or take a few trillion, but
“the spread of the Western lifestyle

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.960
has been accompanied
by microbial changes,”

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:34.760
which may be contributing to our
epidemics of chronic disease.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:38.160
The problem is that we’re
eating these meat-sweet diets,

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:41.000
characterized by a high intake
of animal products, sugars,

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.480
processed foods, and a low
intake of whole plant foods.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:48.880
Contrary to the fermentation of
the carbohydrates that make it down

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:52.600
to our colon—the fiber and
resistant starch that benefit us

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:55.720
through the generation of these
magical short chain fatty acids

00:00:55.720 --> 00:01:00.000
like butyrate—microbial
protein fermentation,

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.080
when excess protein is consumed…
that generates potentially toxic

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:08.560
and pro-carcinogenic metabolites
involved in colorectal cancer.

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:11.320
And so, what we eat
can cause an imbalance

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:14.480
in our gut microbiome and
potentially create a ‘recipe’

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:18.000
for colorectal cancer,
where a high-fat, high-meat,

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.000
high processed food diet tips the scale

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.080
towards dysbiosis and
colorectal cancer,

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:28.080
whereas a high-fiber and starch,
lower meat diet can pull you back

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:33.520
into symbiosis with your friendly
flora and away from cancer.

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:35.800
We now have evidence from
interventional studies

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:40.200
suggesting that “adopting a plant-based,
minimally processed high-fiber diet

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.960
may rapidly reverse the effects of

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:44.880
meat-based diets on
the gut microbiome.”

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:48.600
So, what may be a new form of
personalized microbiome

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.200
medicine for chronic disease?

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:55.520
It’s called food, which can
rapidly and reproducibly

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:57.960
alter the human gut microbiome.

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:00.360
Switch people between a whole
food plant-based diet

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.840
and more of an animal
food-based diet,

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:05.840
and you can see dramatic
shifts within two days,

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:08.640
which can result in
toxic metabolites.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:10.680
Switch people to an
animal food-based diet

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:13.400
and levels of deoxycholic
acid go up,

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:16.000
which is a secondary bile
acid known to promote

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:19.000
DNA damage and liver cancers.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:21.000
Why do levels go up?

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.880
Because the bad bacteria
producing the stuff

00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:27.680
triple—in just two days.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.840
And over time the richness
of the microbial diversity

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:33.440
in our gut is disappearing.

00:02:33.440 --> 00:02:38.680
Here’s our bacterial tree of
life that’s getting depleted.

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:40.520
Why is this happening?

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:42.160
The fiber gap.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:47.640
“A low-fiber diet is a key
driver of microbiome depletion.”

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:50.040
Yeah, there’s antibiotics,
and cesarean sections,

00:02:50.040 --> 00:02:52.200
and indoor plumbing,
but the only factor

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:55.720
that has been empirically
demonstrated to be important

00:02:55.720 --> 00:03:00.560
is a diet low in MACs
(not Big Macs),

00:03:00.560 --> 00:03:04.120
microbiota-accessible carbohydrates,

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:05.440
which is just a fancy name

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:08.760
for fiber found in a whole
plant foods and resistant starch

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:12.440
found mostly in beans, peas,
lentils, and whole grains.

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:15.640
Our intake of dietary fiber,
our intake of whole plant foods,

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:18.320
is negligibly low
in the Western world

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:22.640
when compared to what we evolved
to eat over millions of years.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.440
Such a low-fiber diet provides
insufficient nutrients for

00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:29.400
our gut microbes, leading
not only to the loss

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.520
of bacterial diversity and richness,

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:33.640
but also to the reduction
in the production

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:36.160
of those beneficial
fermentation end products

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:38.960
that they make with the fiber.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:44.560
We are in effect, starving
our microbial self.

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:47.200
What are we going to do about
the deleterious consequences

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:50.360
of a diet deficient
in whole plant foods?

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:53.920
Create new-fangled functional foods,
of course, and supplements,

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:56.960
and drugs—prebiotics,
probiotics, synbiotics.

00:03:56.960 --> 00:03:59.720
Think how much money
there is to be made!

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:06.760
Or, we could just eat the way
our bodies were meant to eat.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:11.200
What kind of value is that going
to get your stockholders, though?

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.880
Don’t you know probiotic
pills may be the next

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:17.800
big source of big
pharma billions?

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:20.840
Why eat healthy though, when
you can just have someone else

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:24.720
eat healthy for you and
then get a fecal transplant

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:26.440
from a vegan!

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:30.040
Researchers compared the microbiomes
of vegans versus omnivores,

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:32.800
and found the vegan’s friendly
flora were churning out

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:35.440
more of the good stuff,
showing that a plant-based diet

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:38.560
may result in more beneficial
metabolites in the bloodstream

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:41.560
and less of the bad
stuff like TMAO.

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:43.280
But while the impact
of a vegan diet

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:46.080
on what the bacteria
were making was large,

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:50.040
the effect on the composition
of the gut microbiome

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:52.320
was surprisingly modest.

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:55.680
They only found “slight differences
between the gut microbiomes

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:58.600
of omnivores versus vegans”?

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:00.680
That was a shocker to the researchers;

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:04.400
this very modest difference
juxtaposed against

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:06.880
the significantly enhanced
dietary consumption

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:08.960
of fermentable plant foods.

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:12.600
The vegans were eating
nearly twice the fiber.

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.840
Anyone see the problem here?

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:19.560
The vegans just barely made the
minimum daily intake of fiber.

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:20.600
Why?

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:24.320
Because Oreos are vegan,
Cocoa Pebbles are vegan,

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:28.360
french fries, Coke, potato chips,
there are vegan Doritos and Pop-Tarts.

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:31.800
You can eat a terrible vegan diet.

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:35.360
Burkitt showed that you need
to get at least 50 grams a day

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:38.120
(of fiber) for colon
cancer prevention.

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:42.080
That’s only half of what our
bodies were designed to get.

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:45.920
We evolved getting
about 100 grams a day.

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:47.880
And that’s what you see
in modern populations

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:50.880
that are immune to
epidemic colorectal cancer.

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:53.440
So, what if instead of
feeding people a vegan diet,

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:55.680
you just fed people
that kind of diet,

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:59.720
a diet centered around
whole plant foods?

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:05.000
We’ll find out next.

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:09.360
Colon cancer is our second
leading cancer killer,

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:11.200
but some places,like rural Africa,

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:14.360
have more than 10 times
lower rates than we do.

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:16.440
The reason we know it’s
not genetic is that

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:19.920
“migrant studies, such as
those in Japanese Hawaiians,

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:22.520
have demonstrated that it
only takes one generation

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:23.800
for the immigrant population

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:25.840
to assume the colon
cancer incidence

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:28.600
of the host Western population.”

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:30.920
Now, the change in
diet is considered

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:32.840
most probably responsible for this.

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:34.560
But there are all
sorts of changes

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.520
when you move from
one culture to another—

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:39.240
like smoking rates, different
exposures to chemicals,

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:40.600
infections, antibiotics.

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:43.320
You don’t know if it’s the diet…

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:46.760
until you put it to the test.

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:49.640
It's rare I do a whole
video on a single study,

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:53.360
but I think you’ll agree
this one is worth it.

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:55.240
This international group of researchers

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:57.840
were trying to find out
why colon cancer rates

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:00.680
were an order of
magnitude higher here—

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:03.160
in African Americans and Caucasians—

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:05.640
than in rural Africa.

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:09.640
Well, if you look at American
colons, they’re a mess:

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:12.520
polyps, diverticulosis—
not to mention hemorrhoids—

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:16.080
whereas the African colons
were remarkably pristine.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.600
And more importantly,
sevenfold lower

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:22.120
colonic epithelial
proliferation rates,

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:25.960
a characteristic of
precancerous conditions.

00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:28.760
They measured everything
that they were eating

00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:31.400
and concluded that the higher
colorectal cancer risk

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:34.120
and proliferation rates
were most closely

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:37.800
“associated with higher dietary
intakes of animal products”,

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:40.200
which may have led to
“higher colonic populations

00:07:40.200 --> 00:07:42.080
of these potentially toxic [acid]

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:45.120
and bile-salt-producing bacteria.”

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:46.640
But you don’t know…

00:07:46.640 --> 00:07:49.000
until you put it to the test.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:51.360
Higher rates are
associated with higher

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:52.960
animal protein and animal fat,

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:56.240
lower fiber consumption,
more of those bad bile acids,

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:59.240
less of those good short chain
fatty acids like butyrate,

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:01.640
and that higher
mucosal proliferation.

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:04.880
But how do we know it’s the
diet that’s mucking things up?

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:05.600
You don’t know…

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:09.520
until you perform an
interventional study.

00:08:09.520 --> 00:08:12.400
How about we just
swap their diets?

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:15.200
Feed the Americans a high-
fiber African-style diet,

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:17.400
and those poor Africans get the SAD,

00:08:17.400 --> 00:08:19.040
Standard American Diet,

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:21.780
like sausage and white flour
pancakes for breakfast,

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:23.360
a burger and fries for lunch,

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:26.640
and like some meatloaf
and white rice for supper.

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:29.800
That was day one for the rural
Africans in the experiment,

00:08:29.800 --> 00:08:32.240
whereas the Americans
were forced to eat

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:35.240
fruits and vegetables,
corn and beans.

00:08:35.240 --> 00:08:37.680
To help with compliance they
threw in more familiar foods

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:41.520
like veggie dogs, though
note it was not a vegan diet,

00:08:41.520 --> 00:08:43.840
just generally plant-based.

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:46.240
And the food exchanges
weren’t for years,

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:48.080
but just two weeks.

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:50.600
Could they see changes that fast?

00:08:50.600 --> 00:08:53.480
The dietary changes
resulted in remarkable

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:56.160
reciprocal changes in the
lining of their colons

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:59.400
in terms of cancer risk
and their microbiome.

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:02.480
Switching to plant-based boosted
the fiber fermentation

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:06.280
and suppressed the carcinogenic
bile acid synthesis.

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:09.040
Let’s look at some before
and after pictures.

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:12.800
They took biopsies, and
this is the colon lining

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:15.520
of an African American
under a microscope.

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:18.880
Those brown dots
mark dividing cells;

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:21.440
their colon lining was in overdrive,

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:23.200
the cells rapidly dividing,

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:26.880
a sign of premalignancy,
a risk factor for cancer.

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:29.720
But just two weeks
eating a healthier diet,

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:33.440
and their colons calmed right down.

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:38.040
The African Africans started
out with some proliferation,

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:41.680
but it got worse on
the American diet.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:44.320
This is a different marker
measuring inflammation.

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:47.720
Each of the brown dots here
represents an inflammatory cell;

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:51.840
so, rife inflammation before
calmed way down after

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:53.120
just two weeks,

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:56.800
and the opposite in
those eating worse.

00:09:56.800 --> 00:10:00.000
We know that when our friendly
flora ferment fiber,

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.120
they produce beneficial
compounds like butyrate,

00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:04.600
which is anti-inflammatory
and anti-cancer.

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:08.240
Well, impressively,
‘Africanization’ of the diet

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:10.440
more than doubled butyrate production,

00:10:10.440 --> 00:10:13.600
whereas ‘Westernization’ cut it in half.

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:17.640
In terms of toxic metabolites,
a significant drop on the healthier diet,

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:20.280
whereas the ‘meatloafy’
diet increased the levels

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:24.800
of these carcinogens by 400%
within just two weeks.

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:28.160
So, bottom line (no pun intended):

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:32.680
what they were able to show is
that just by changing the food,

00:10:32.680 --> 00:10:35.200
you can remarkably
change your risk.

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:37.360
In fact, that’s how the
lead investigator put it:

00:10:37.360 --> 00:10:39.800
“change your diet,
change your cancer risk!”

00:10:39.800 --> 00:10:44.160
It may be never too late
to start eating healthier.

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:47.280
Based on these kind of data,
“adopting a whole-food vegan

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:50.040
or [even just] near-vegan diet
rich in fruits and vegetables,”

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:52.200
along with other healthy
lifestyle decisions,

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:54.360
“could have a stunningly
positive impact

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:56.680
on the cancer risks not
only of black Americans,

00:10:56.680 --> 00:10:58.320
but of all peoples.”

00:10:58.320 --> 00:11:01.080
“While it [might] be
unrealistic to expect

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:03.040
rapid and profound lifestyle changes

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:05.160
in the general population,
[hey]…at least we have

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:09.280
sound, effective advice to offer
to those who [make the choice]

00:11:09.280 --> 00:11:17.446
to take the steps needed to
optimize their healthful longevity.”

